  "comments": "The manuscript (ID:5856) contains two parts, entitled respectively \"bslab btus kyi bsgom don dpe'i khrid zab po\" and \"spyod 'jug 'khor lo lta bu'i lam mdor bsdus pa.\" They describe respectively shortly the contents of the chapters of the \u015aik\u1e63\u0101samuccaya (ID:3742) and of the Bodhicary\u0101vat\u0101ra (ID:3727). \r\nThere is a single transmission lineage for both works at the end in (ID:4840), the work reports a teaching transmitted in a lineage starting with Maitreya, down to sKyo ston (ID:4052), and written down in the course of its transmission to Chos kyi rgyal mtshan (ID:6458).\r\nHowever, the colophon of the second part names the author as \"lha btsun pa,\" a scholar active at mChad kha dgon, who may be different from sKyo ston.",
  "alternative_names": "bslab btus kyi bsgom don dpe'i khrid zab po\r\nspyod 'jug 'khor lo lta bu'i lam mdor bsdus pa",
